{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "In the absence of further information, the proposal is considered likely to result in unneighbourly levels of noise generation, increased comings-and-goings and general disturbances, to the extent that this would constitute undue harm to the living conditions of neighbouring occupiers.&nbsp;The proposal is therefore found to be at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that development proposals adequately protect residential amenity:National Planning Policy Framework (December 2023) Policies GG3, D6 (part D) and D14 of the London Plan (March 2021) Policies BR13, BP8 and BP11 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011) Policies DMD1 and DMSI3 of&nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)",
    "The proposed development fails to demonstrate&nbsp;that additional demand for parking from the development could be adequately accommodated in the surrounding area.&nbsp;The proposal is therefore likely to add unacceptably to parking stress and congestion in the vicinity of the application site, and to have a negative impact on highway safety.&nbsp; As such, it fails to comply with the following policies&nbsp;which seek to ensure that proposals show how car parking will be designed and managed, to take into consideration on-street parking availability and existing and planned public transport provision, and to not negatively impact highway safety in particular through pedestrian and vehicular conflict:National Planning Policy Framework&nbsp;(December 2023)Policies T1 and T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policy CP3 of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010)Policies&nbsp;BP8, BP11, BR9 and&nbsp;BR11&nbsp;of the&nbsp;Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)Policies SP2, SP8 and DMT2 of&nbsp;The London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan: (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021)"
  ],
